mmendation to Candidate B, or at least suggest we need to compare C vs B on stress resilience and crew cooperation. Since we have explicit evidence that B handles stress well, that fills a gap. Also B is very conscientious (reliability). But B has concerns about communication tone and pretentiousness, which may affect crew cooperation.\n\nWe could argue that stress resilience is a must-have, and lacking evidence for C is a serious gap, while B has explicit evidence. So we might shift vote to B, but we need to consider other criteria.\n\nWe could also ask about Candidate D's stress resilience, but we have \"responds to unexpected events adequately\" which may indicate some resilience but not explicit.\n\nGiven the need to cover all candidates, we could bring up Candidate B now, compare with C, and maybe shift provisional recommendation to B, but note concerns.\n\nThus Emily's public message: \"I agree that C is strong, but we lack stress resilience evidence. Since B is documented to handle stress very well, and is very conscientious, I think B may be a stronger overall fit despite some communication concerns. I propose we shift provisional recommendation to Candidate B, pending further discussion on crew cooperation.\"\n\nWe need to reference Sarah's answer. Provide evidence: B handles stress very well (from Emily's notes). Also B is very conscientious (reliability). Provide concerns: pretentious, wrong tone.\n\nThus vote for Candidate B.\n\nProceed."}
