cerns: B's uncooperative behavior vs C's communication difficulty. Also we still need to discuss Candidate A and D. We need to bring up another candidate or probe missing criteria. According to process, we should discuss another candidate, maybe A or D. Since A hasn't been discussed, we could introduce A, compare with C. Provide evidence: A anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership, but regarded as a show\u2011off, not open to new ideas. Also concerns about reliability (unorganized) and cooperation (not good at taking criticism). We could argue that A's technical competence is strong but reliability and cooperation concerns are serious. So we may keep C as provisional but note A is less suitable. Or we could ask about stress resilience for A or D. But we can bring up A now.\n\nThus James Carter should make a contribution: perhaps say \"I agree with Sarah that C remains the best provisional, but we still need to evaluate Candidate A's technical strengths vs his reliability concerns.\" Provide evidence: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership, but regarded as a show\u2011off and not open to new ideas, can be unorganized. Conclude that A's reliability concerns outweigh technical strengths for long-distance pilot, so C remains best. Also note we still need to discuss D later.\n\nThus vote remains Candidate C.\n\nProceed to output."}
